#####################################################################
# Confluent Cloud Connection Configuration                          #
#                                                                   #
# Note: The plugin supports different ways of passing parameters:   #
# - Programmatically                                                #
# - Via global environment variables                                #
# - Via arguments in the main() method                              #
# - Via properties file                                             #
#                                                                   #
# For all cases, use the ConfluentSettings class to get started.    #
#                                                                   #
# The project is preconfigured with this properties file.           #
#####################################################################

# Cloud region
#client.cloud=aws
#client.region=eu-west-1

# Compute resources
#client.organization-id=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
#client.environment-id=env-xxxxx
#client.compute-pool-id=lfcp-xxxxxxxxxx

# Target catalog and database: the default environment and Kafka cluster that unqualified table
# names resolve to (equivalent to env.useCatalog(...) / env.useDatabase(...) in code).
#   - sql.current-catalog:  a Confluent environment name (or ID).
#   - sql.current-database: a Kafka cluster name (or ID) within that environment.
# Examples that create tables, register functions, or submit statements require these, and the API
# key set below must have WRITE access to the Kafka cluster. Each example's docstring says whether
# it writes.
#sql.current-catalog=MyEnv
#sql.current-database=my_db

# --- Secrets (keep these out of any committed file) ---
# A single global (Cloud) API key covers both Flink access and artifact uploads.
# See README "Authentication" for all options.
# Supply via .env instead if you wish to commit this properties file to git
#client.global-api-key=
#client.global-api-secret=